    prior: {
      itemId: 'item.4fa776b35f0b',
      locator: {
        kind: 'numbered-item',
        anchor:
          'md-block:# Spec-Driven Development Convention > ## 5. The Spec ↔ Jira Contract:list-item:4',
        lineHint: 219,
      },
      normalizedExcerpt:
        '4. Conflicts resolve as follows: Jira wins on delivery state (priority, schedule, assignment); the spec wins on implementation detail. If they disagree on scope, work **stops** until a human reconciles them. Agents do not adjudicate scope conflicts.',
      valueDigest: 'ee9999770ae466b56bfc7c9543ef0989a3db40020502a3ffa61ef4480d584f94',
      ruleIds: ['rule.spec-convention.4fa776b35f0b'],
      exclusionDisposition: null,
      rationale:
        'Rule-bearing section or live behavior is mapped to an explicit source-bound rule.',
    },
    current: {
      itemId: 'item.4fa776b35f0b',
      locator: {
        kind: 'numbered-item',
        anchor:
          'md-block:# Spec-Driven Development Convention > ## 5. The Spec ↔ Jira Contract:list-item:4',
        lineHint: 221,
      },
      normalizedExcerpt:
        '4. Conflicts resolve as follows: Jira wins on delivery state (priority, schedule, assignment); the spec wins on implementation detail. Under OM-PAN-001, versioned goal/parcel IDs and Git/PR evidence are canonical; unavailable Jira/Linear fields are explicitly not applicable. The coordinator reconciles stale projections; conflicting material authority is an exception. Other scope conflicts stop for human reconciliation.',
      valueDigest: '0bda6bd67ead17e18ab4df5db2bb0c79931d21c09d4518dfe573579c3446277b',
      ruleIds: ['rule.spec-convention.4fa776b35f0b', 'rule.r34.spec-convention.4fa776b35f0b'],
      exclusionDisposition: null,
      rationale:
        'R34 Pantheon-only clause retained as non-operative narrative. This resolver cannot admit Pantheon or broaden Foreman Kernel authority. Existing generic clauses retain their separately mapped rules.',
    },
