        "Under Clinton Morgan's transferable Context oversight/process authorization, the originating oversight session approves this administrative exception for `collective-civilizational-memory` parcels **CCM-P1A, CCM-P1B, CCM-P1C and CCM-P1D only**, during local foundation development. It changes no locked product decision. For these four parcels, the CCM foundation ledger in `docs/specs/INDEX.md` is the delivery-state record instead of Jira; the existing CCM ticket/filename keys remain valid under §§2/4/5. Each ledger entry records status, accountable owner, dependencies, exact spec repository/path/commit and SHA-256, actual tree-approval record/hash, Gate 2 decision, named worktree/branch and evidence links. The assigned work order names the ledger path and parcel key; dispatch pins the committed ledger revision. The ledger pins the spec revision separately, avoiding a circular pair of mutually self-referential commit hashes. Material spec changes require refreshed spec pins and renewed applicable approval; ledger status changes never grant authority.",
