      normalizedExcerpt:
        "The coordinator runs as a self-pacing loop (`/goal` enters it after ratification): work while there is work, sleep on a long fallback while builders build (completion notifications are the primary wake signal), stop when the exit criterion is met or a stop condition fires. One goal, one coordinator: the loop directive carries an ownership block, and outside a verified succession mandate, ownership transfers only at parcel boundaries via that block; OM-PAN-001 instead uses its explicit initial transfer, then transactional lease/CAS and effect-side fencing after service acceptance (rule earned when a second coordinator committed onto a live parcel branch - 491fb80 - and was benign only by luck). OM-PAN-001 evidence failures hold dependent actions with bounded recovery and independent work continuing; queue exhaustion never proves exits met. Outside that scoped policy, universal stop conditions: a frozen contract needs modification; a tripwire fires twice on one parcel; a security finding can't close in-parcel; anything outward-facing beyond the standing authorizations; queue empty.",
